Logic Puzzles (apps/puzzles)

Puzzles (engine/, help/, icons/)
  Simon Tatham's Portable Puzzle Collection, by Simon Tatham, with portions
  by Richard Boulton, James Harvey, Mike Pinna, Jonas Kölker, Dariusz
  Olszewski, Michael Schierl, Lambros Lambrou, Bernd Schmidt, Steffen Bauer,
  Lennard Sprong, Rogier Goossens, Michael Quevillon, Asher Gordon, Didi
  Kohen, Ben Harris and Anders Höglund.
  License: MIT (engine/LICENCE.txt).
  Source: https://git.tartarus.org/simon/puzzles.git, commit
  616da16f25da428ccda805536209095bd062676e, with frunk.store's changes for
  this screen in engine/puzzles-web.patch (also tools/puzzles/puzzles-web.patch
  in https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose tools/build-puzzles.mjs
  builds it).
  The changes: the page is told after every move (to keep the game and
  update its keys); web_keys() lists the keys a puzzle wants on screen,
  web_key() and web_cursor() press them, and web_status() says whether the
  puzzle is solved; each puzzle keeps its own preferences; and Guess
  redraws all of the area under a dragged peg, so the peg leaves no trail.
  The help pages are the collection's manual (puzzles.but), one chapter per
  puzzle, made into HTML by Halibut. The icons are drawn by the puzzles
  themselves from the collection's icon saves (icons/*.sav), cropped as
  its icons/icons.cmake crops them.

The rest of apps/puzzles (the page, its touch controls and the icon.svg)
is part of frunk.store.
